lesson: 137
title: Brackets in a story: first the group, then the groups
level: primary-2
stars: 1
explain: Work out what is in brackets first. In 3 × (4 + 2) we first find 4 + 2 = 6, then 3 × 6 = 18.
explain: A story for it: 3 bags, each with 4 red and 2 green apples. One bag has 4 + 2 = 6 apples, so 3 bags have 3 × 6 = 18.
explain: Counting the colours apart gives the same: 3 × 4 + 3 × 2 = 12 + 6 = 18.
vars: a=name k=2..6 x=2..9 y=2..9
answer: k * (x + y)
exercise: {a} buys {k} bags. In each bag there are {x} red apples and {y} green apples. How many apples does {a.he} buy?
exercise: Each of {k} vases holds {x} roses and {y} tulips. How many flowers are in the vases?
exercise: {a} reads {x} pages in the morning and {y} pages in the evening, every day for {k} days. How many pages does {a.he} read?
exercise: A pack has {x} pencils and {y} pens. {a} buys {k} packs. How many pencils and pens does {a.he} buy in all?
exercise: {k} children each bring {x} cookies and {y} candies to a party. How many cookies and candies do they bring altogether?
exercise: A box holds {x} big buttons and {y} small buttons. How many buttons are there in {k} such boxes?
test: Every week {a} saves {x} dollars of {a.his} pocket money and gets {y} dollars more from {a.his} grandmother. How many dollars has {a.he} put by after {k} weeks?
test: In each of {k} rows of a garden grow {x} carrots and {y} beets. Count all the vegetables in the garden.
test: A ticket costs {x} dollars for the ride and {y} dollars for the zoo. What do {k} children pay to go to both?
test: {k} friends each buy a sandwich for {x} dollars and a juice for {y} dollars. How much do the friends spend in all?
exercise: How many apples does {a} buy altogether, if {a.he} buys {k} bags with {x} red and {y} green apples in each?
exercise: {k} baskets. Each: {x} plums and {y} pears. How many pieces of fruit in total?
exercise: A florist in Seattle makes {k} bunches, each with {x} daisies and {y} lilies. How many flowers does she use in all?
exercise: {a} packs {k.words} lunch boxes for a trip in Scotland, putting {x.words} crackers and {y.words} grapes in every box. How many crackers and grapes are packed altogether?
exercise: Each of {k} shelves in a library in Ottawa has {x} storybooks and {y} comics. How many books are on the shelves combined?
exercise: {a} practises the piano for {x} minutes and the violin for {y} minutes every day. How many minutes does {a.he} practise in {k} days?
exercise: A team in Queensland has {x} boys and {y} girls. How many players are there in {k} such teams?
exercise: Every gift bag holds {y} stickers and {x} badges. How many stickers and badges are there in {k} gift bags?
test: What is the total number of birds in {k} cages, if every cage in a pet shop in Texas has {x} parrots and {y} canaries?
test: {k} school buses in Wales each carry {x} teachers and {y} parents. How many adults ride the buses?
test: {a} earns {x} dollars a day for walking dogs and {y} dollars a day for washing cars. What does {a.he} earn in {k} days?
test: Count the cups and plates: {k} picnic sets, with {x} cups and {y} plates apiece.
test: In Wellington, a coach carries {x} footballs and {y} netballs to every one of {k} training days. How many balls are carried in all?
test: At a café in Cork, {k.words} tables each have {x.words} chairs and {y.words} stools. Find the number of seats.
exercise: {a} got {k} bags, {x} red apples n {y} green in each. how many apples
exercise: {k+1} vases — sorry, {k} vases, each got {x} roses and {y} tulips. how many flowers
exercise: my mate did {k} × {x} + {y} = {k*x+y}. nah thats not it, how many apples in {k} bags of {x} red and {y} green
exercise: {a} reads {x} pages in the morning, {y} at night, every day for {k} days, the book's like 300 pages. how many pages {a.he} read
test: each kid gets {x} pencils and {y} rubbers, {k} kids. how many things altogether
test: {k} boxes with {x} big cookies n {y} small ones each, how many cookies total
test: {a} reckons {k} plates of {x} sandwiches and {y} cakes is {k+x+y} things. nah. how many really
exam: It is given that {a} purchases {k} bags, each containing {x} red apples and {y} green apples. Determine the aggregate number of apples purchased.
exam: Whereas each of {k} vases contains {x} roses and {y} tulips, ascertain the total number of flowers in the vases.
exam: {a} reads {x} pages in the morning and {y} pages in the evening on each of {k} consecutive days. State the total number of pages so read.
exam: Compute the product of {k} and the sum of {x} and {y}.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left a little tin for each of her {k} grandchildren, with {x} old marbles and {y} old buttons inside. How many marbles and buttons did she leave in all?
exercise: Since Dad was let go, the family eats cheaply: each week they buy {x} kg of rice and {y} kg of potatoes. How many kilograms of food is that over {k} weeks?
test: {a}'s been telling porkies, says "only a couple". crap, mate — {x} sweets and {y} biscuits every single day for {k} days. how many snacks did the greedy guts put away?
